#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# weierstrass_sigma

#% text
# `weierstrass_sigma(u, [g2, g3])` gives the Weierstrass sigma function `sigma(u; g2, g3)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `sigma` is the entire odd function with simple zeros at the lattice points, `sigma'/sigma = zeta` and `sigma'(0) = 1` (DLMF 23.2.6).

#% item
# Numerical values come from `sigma(u) = (2 omega1/pi) exp(eta1 u^2/(2 omega1)) theta_1(v)/theta_1'(0)`, `v = pi u/(2 omega1)` (DLMF 23.6.9), with the quasi-periodicity of DLMF 23.2.20 for arguments outside the period parallelogram.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
weierstrass_sigma(0.5, [1, 2])
#% output
#= 0.499851177908916

#% cell
n(weierstrass_sigma(1/3, [1, 2]), 30)
#% output
#= 0.3333150975525210008724751746227234

#% cell
weierstrass_sigma(7.3 - 4.1*im, [1, 2])
#% output
#= -32103335.552030552 - 4558452.705663622im

#% cell
weierstrass_sigma(u, [0, 0])
#% output
#= u

